+# Optional local adapter contract (non-normative)
+
+This is harness transport version `airep-k2-local-1`, not an AIREP schema or release.
+It carries the existing #62 artifact/verification inputs. An adapter must implement
+its own producer or consumer logic. It is not required to import the reference
+verifier, use Python, or reproduce its output format. Adapters are supplied only
+when a contributor has a concrete implementation to measure.
+
+## Configuration and invocation
+
+Pass `--producer-adapter /absolute/path/producer.json` and/or
+`--consumer-adapter /absolute/path/consumer.json` to `harness.py run`.
+The JSON configuration contains:
+
+```json
+{
+  "role": "consumer",
+  "target": "COPY THE EXACT OBJECT FROM pins.json.target",
+  "implementation_id": "contributor-implementation-and-version",
+  "argv": ["/absolute/path/to/consumer-adapter"],
+  "source_file": "/absolute/path/to/declared-source-snapshot",
+  "source_sha256": "64 lowercase hex characters"
+}
+```
+
+`target` above is a placeholder: replace it with the JSON object, not a string.
+`argv` is executed directly, without a shell, in the config file's directory.
+The source_file can be a contributor-created archive of the complete source;
+the harness hashes its exact bytes before execution. This check alone cannot
+verify that the program actually implements the declared source. Bundle its
+licence, dependency closure, toolchain versions and method note for human review.
+
+The process reads one UTF-8 JSON request from stdin and writes exactly one UTF-8
+JSON response to stdout. Send diagnostic text to stderr. The harness preserves
+both streams and exit code, rejects duplicate JSON keys, and uses a 180 s timeout.
+Nonzero exit, timeout, missing executable, wrong target/role or hash mismatch can
+never become a successful result. Missing configuration is
+`EXTERNAL_RESULT_NOT_SUPPLIED`; an unavailable configured executable is
+`ADAPTER_UNAVAILABLE`.
+
+The request contains `adapter_contract`, `role`, the exact `target` object,
+`output_dir`, `input_bundle` and `input_manifest_sha256`. The last two are null
+for a producer. Absolute paths are local to this invocation.
+
+Every response contains the same `target`, `role` and `implementation_id` as the
+configuration. The response is retained separately from reference outputs.
+
+## Producer
+
+Write these files inside `output_dir/bundle/`:
+
+| File | Content |
+|---|---|
+| lifecycle.json | Array of five wire-version `0.2` artifacts: Decision, issuer dispatched Control, receiver received Control, Execution, Effect |
+| bindings.json | Explicit contributor-controlled test-key bindings using the pinned verification contract |
+| revocation.json | Explicit test revocation input using the pinned verification contract |
+| independence.json | Explicit test policy; empty pairs may leave independence unknown |
+| bundle.json | Manifest below |
+
+```json
+{
+  "target": "COPY pins.json.target OBJECT",
+  "implementation_id": "same ID as configuration",
+  "files": {
+    "lifecycle.json": "SHA-256 of exact file bytes",
+    "bindings.json": "SHA-256 of exact file bytes",
+    "revocation.json": "SHA-256 of exact file bytes",
+    "independence.json": "SHA-256 of exact file bytes"
+  },
+  "profile_basis": null,
+  "authorship": "UNASSESSED"
+}
+```
+
+No canonicalization is performed for these file hashes. A whitespace change must
+change the hash. No profiles are accepted by this deliberately minimal transport.
+After a valid response the harness consumes the bundle with the pinned reference
+tools and, if provided, the external consumer. Admission, authentication,
+reconciliation and process errors remain separate evidence.
+
+## Consumer
+
+Read the four declared input files and bundle manifest; preserve their bytes.
+Return `input_manifest_sha256` exactly as received, plus `native_result` containing
+your own JSON result. Your own classification can report failure, unknown or an
+ambiguity; it does not need to resemble the reference output. Reusing the reference
+engine would need disclosure and would not demonstrate an independent consumer.
+
+An optional `observation` enables mechanical comparison. Omit it or set it to null
+when the result cannot honestly map to this projection; comparison then remains
+`NOT_COMPARABLE`. The projection has exactly three keys:
+
+- `records`: array sorted by `record_id`, with `record_id`, `class`,
+  `authenticated_failures`, `authenticated_withheld`, `witnessed_withheld`,
+  `observer_assessment` mapped to the pinned verification meanings.
+- `reconciliation_summary`: the pinned reconciliation `status` and five `counts`.
+- `checks`: array of `{check, subject, state}`, sorted by UTF-8 bytes of Python
+  `json.dumps(item, ensure_ascii=False, sort_keys=True, indent=2) + LF`.
+
+When `observation` is supplied, validation is recursive and fail-closed. It
+must have exactly those three keys. `records` and `checks` must be arrays; each
+element must contain exactly the fields listed above. Record IDs are nonempty,
+unique, admitted Unicode strings sorted by record_id. Class values are exactly
+`AIREP-Core`, `AIREP-Authenticated`, `AIREP-Witnessed`; observer values are exactly
+`same_executor`, `independent`, `unknown`, `not_applicable`. Reason arrays must be
+deduplicated ASCII-sorted strings from their exact tier/channel in the frozen
+CLASS_VERIFIER_CONTRACT.md §5. The projected class/reason invariants from §2 apply.
+
+`reconciliation_summary` has exactly `status` and `counts`. Status is `FAILURE`,
+`INCOMPLETE` or `SATISFIED`. Counts has exactly `SATISFIED`, `FAILURE`, `MISSING`,
+`NOT_EVALUATED`, `INDETERMINATE`, each a nonnegative integer (not a Boolean or
+floating-point number). Counts must equal the supplied checks, and status follows
+the frozen failure/incomplete/satisfied precedence. Check names and structured
+subject identities must use the pinned reconciler vocabulary; states use exactly
+the five count labels. No unknown fields, null nested structures or fabricated
+vocabulary are accepted. Source hashes are in
+`sources/projection-validation-source.json`.
+
+Malformed supplied projections yield `ADAPTER_ERROR` with
+`MALFORMED_COMPARISON_PROJECTION` before the adapter result can be `REPORTED` or
+compared. The exact response bytes remain retained. An omitted or null
+`observation` still yields `NOT_COMPARABLE`; a consumer can always retain its
+native result without claiming that it fits the optional projection.
+
+The optional normalization vocabulary is defined by the release documents; its
+implementation is yours. Exact equality yields `PROJECTION_AGREES`; unequal
+projections yield `PROJECTION_DIVERGES`. Neither word establishes conformance or
+independent authorship. Original native_result and command output are always
+retained. A failed reference process yields `REFERENCE_PROCESS_ERROR` rather than
+a comparison. Mappings that cannot be made are never silently guessed.
+
+## Evidence boundary
+
+No adapter is supplied in this package. Unit tests create local protocol test
+doubles, explicitly labelled as such, and never add their outputs to external
+evidence. A real contributor still owes the source/licence, toolchain, artifact
+hashes, command logs, method note and maintainer reproduction described in #62.
