+# Same-version local interop harness — v0.2.0-beta.1
+
+This non-normative package makes [issue #62](https://github.com/halvrenofviryel/ai-runtime-evidence-protocol/issues/62)
+runnable without changing its challenge. It fixes every role to release
+`v0.2.0-beta.1`, commit `8a6c01ecce457aa94330c0ed7219e4c56ebfe771`, wire version `0.2`.
+It adds a local transport contract, role matrix, automated measurements and evidence
+separation. It does not implement an independently authored producer or verifier.
+
+The package and test doubles were authored with AI assistance. First-party producer,
+verifier and reconciler source was read and is reused explicitly for the reference
+lane. Nothing here is a submission to issue #62 or a new entry in EXTERNAL_EVIDENCE.md.
+
+## Run
+
+From the repository root, use an output directory that does not exist:
+
+```sh
+python3 interop/same-version/v0.2.0-beta.1/harness.py produce --out /tmp/k2-produced
+python3 interop/same-version/v0.2.0-beta.1/harness.py run --local-bundle /tmp/k2-produced/local-reference-bundle --out /tmp/k2-measured
+```
+
+Or generate and measure in one command:
+
+```sh
+python3 interop/same-version/v0.2.0-beta.1/harness.py run --out /tmp/k2-combined
+python3 -m unittest discover -s interop/same-version/v0.2.0-beta.1 -p 'test_*.py' -v
+```
+
+Python 3.12 on Linux x86-64 and Node are required. This run measured Python 3.12.3
+and Node 20.19.6. `pins.json` contains frozen dependency manifests and SHA-256
+identities. The runner archives the exact release commit from local Git, verifies
+the archive plus individual normative/source/dependency files, and materializes
+the release's offline bundles in a fresh temporary directory. It never installs
+from an index and never runs the current main-branch verifier by accident.
+
+The fresh release directory is retained and named in `run_record.json`. Dependency
+setup must be able to launch child processes. The original sandbox restriction
+(`spawnSync EPERM`) is retained as a failed attempt, separately from the successful
+authorized local rerun.
+
+The five artifacts are Decision, issuer Control dispatch, receiver Control receipt,
+Execution and Effect. The existing release example executes a local file change
+and uses public test keys. Python verification and reconciliation and all five
+Node request evaluations are captured independently. These are reference adapters
+from the same first-party implementation family; parity is not independent authorship.
+
+## Results and claim boundary
+
+The checked-in [RESULTS.md](RESULTS.md) identifies the exact local measurement and
+tests. Detailed argv, cwd, exits, stdout/stderr, input hashes, negative controls and
+role-separated results live in the run record. A successful local harness check
+does not replace the reconciler's `INCOMPLETE` result with PASS. All three external
+lanes remain `EXTERNAL_RESULT_NOT_SUPPLIED` until supplied adapters actually run.
+
+[ROLE_MATRIX.md](ROLE_MATRIX.md) fixes which implementation produces or consumes
+each bundle. [ADAPTER_CONTRACT.md](ADAPTER_CONTRACT.md) describes the small optional
+stdin/stdout adapter. An external consumer can preserve its own native result;
+the reference verifier is not required as its logic or dependency.
+
+External commands are opt-in local executable programs, not sandboxed plugins.
+Their outputs and any optional comparison projections are unassessed reports.
+Source-file hashes bind a declared entry point, not an entire dependency closure
+or contributor identity. Source, licence, exact toolchain, test-key ownership,
+method note and maintainer reproduction required by #62 remain external inputs.
+No third-party independence, general interoperability, real authority, report
+truth, completeness, standards endorsement or production safety is claimed.
+
+This transport accepts only the minimal no-profile lifecycle. It does not change
+normative schemas/protocol rules, expand v0.1 claims, or provide a new challenge.
+
+Code: Apache-2.0, consistent with CONTRIBUTING.md. This tooling documentation does
+not override the repository's CC-BY-4.0 specification/schema licence.
+
+## Complete archived payloads
+
+To keep the review compact, all measurement payloads and logs are retained in
+`evidence/payloads.tar.gz`, with per-file hashes in `evidence/PAYLOAD_SHA256SUMS`.
+The final signed lifecycle, policies, final command streams and run records remain
+directly readable; duplicate generated bundles, raw contribution logs and negative
+fixtures (including deliberately trailing whitespace) are in the archive unchanged.
+
+Restore every captured relative path and verify every payload hash:
+
+```sh
+mkdir /tmp/k2-evidence-restored
+tar -xzf interop/same-version/v0.2.0-beta.1/evidence/payloads.tar.gz -C /tmp/k2-evidence-restored
+# From /tmp/k2-evidence-restored, use the absolute path to the checksum file:
+sha256sum -c /ABSOLUTE/REPO/interop/same-version/v0.2.0-beta.1/evidence/PAYLOAD_SHA256SUMS
+```
+
+The run records retain original execution paths and hashes. The archive preserves
+payload contents, not runtime environments. Reproduce tools with the documented
+commands and frozen dependency bundles.
+
+The external-consumer projection review fix and its new 28-test measurement are
+recorded in [RESULTS.md](RESULTS.md#projection-validation-review-correction).
+The earlier measurement remains unchanged; the real external result is still absent.
