+# K2 same-version local results
+
+**Local package complete; external submission pending.** The reference producer,
+Python verifier/reconciler and Node verifier target `v0.2.0-beta.1`, commit
+`8a6c01ecce457aa94330c0ed7219e4c56ebfe771`. All external lanes remain
+**EXTERNAL_RESULT_NOT_SUPPLIED**. No independent author or outside implementation
+result is claimed.
+
+| Measurement | Actual result |
+|---|---|
+| Minimal lifecycle | Decision, issuer dispatch, receiver receipt, Execution, Effect |
+| Python authentication | Five AIREP-Authenticated records |
+| Python/Node comparison | All five full verdicts equal; same first-party family |
+| Reconciliation | INCOMPLETE: 37 SATISFIED, 1 NOT_EVALUATED, 0 FAILURE/MISSING/INDETERMINATE |
+| Harness tests | 28 current tests, OK; original 20-test result retained |
+| Real negative controls | 8/8 assertions met; negative verdicts retained |
+| Contribution checks | make demo-test and make demo completed; beta check 56/56 commands exit zero |
+
+The reference result's `INCOMPLETE` state is expected because intended-target
+coverage is NOT_EVALUATED. Exit zero means evaluation completed. It is not a
+conformance, truth, completeness or external-independence claim.
+
+## Negative controls
+
+| Control | Preserved outcome |
+|---|---|
+| Whitespace-only byte tamper | BUNDLE_BYTE_HASH_MISMATCH |
+| Manifest target mismatch | TARGET_MISMATCH |
+| Wire-version mismatch after rehash | WIRE_VERSION_MISMATCH |
+| Receiver role rewritten as issuer | CONTROL_ROLE_SEPARATION_MISMATCH |
+| Broken Decision digest | verifier exit 1; reconciler exit 0 with summary FAILURE |
+| Signed TOCTOU mismatch | both commands exit 0; toctou FAILURE and summary FAILURE |
+| No receipt | receiver_receipt MISSING; reconciliation INCOMPLETE |
+| Independence policy omitted | Effect observer_assessment unknown |
+
+The original 20 tests additionally exercise unavailable adapters, nonzero exits carrying a
+fake success response, wrong consumer input hashes, changed source hashes, input
+mutation during consumption, duplicate JSON keys, malformed response/artifact/
+manifest types, role mismatches and real failed verifier/reconciler processes.
+Test doubles are local test code and are not counted as external results.
+
+## Exact commands and evidence
+
+The final two-command producer/measurement flow was executed from the independent
+clone on `codex/airep-v02-same-version-interop`, based on
+`075aff5610731736405951ecf3b7c4bfc3cc0f07`:
+
+```sh
+python3 interop/same-version/v0.2.0-beta.1/harness.py produce --out /tmp/k2-produced-final-r2
+python3 interop/same-version/v0.2.0-beta.1/harness.py run --local-bundle /tmp/k2-produced-final-r2/local-reference-bundle --out interop/same-version/v0.2.0-beta.1/evidence/final-reference
+python3 -m unittest discover -s interop/same-version/v0.2.0-beta.1 -p 'test_*.py' -v
+make demo-test
+make demo 'DEMO_ARGS=--out /tmp/k2-contribution-demo-final'
+python3 scripts/check_beta.py --out /tmp/k2-contribution-beta-final
+```
+
+These output paths already exist in the recorded run; choose new paths when
+repeating. Captured argv use absolute paths where applicable.
+
+- [Common run record](run_record.json): source identities, limits and evidence pointers.
+- [Final measurement](evidence/final-reference/run_record.json): every command/cwd/exit,
+  full textual stdout/stderr, exact bundle bytes and separate role records.
+- [Final command/test logs](evidence/final-validation.json): 20 tests and final two-command run.
+- [Contribution commands](evidence/validation.json) and [beta details](evidence/contribution-beta/results.json).
+- [Pinned sources/dependencies](pins.json), [issue #62 connector snapshot](sources/issue-62-connector.json),
+  [primary docs](sources/primary-documentation.json), [distribution metadata](sources/dependency-metadata.json).
+- [First sandbox attempt](evidence/sandbox-harness-attempt/run_record.json): Node child-process EPERM
+  retained as FAILED. The beta sandbox attempt likewise retained 9 failed commands.
+  Authorized reruns resolved the environment restriction without changing release tools.
+
+The successful final source and dependency versions are Python 3.12.3,
+Node 20.19.6, cryptography 48.0.0 and jsonschema 4.25.1. Every wheel and Node tarball
+is hashed in the frozen manifests; bootstrap verifies them offline. Runtime
+version availability was checked against the linked primary release/documentation
+pages, and dependency package metadata was read from the pinned distributions.
+
+## Scope and remaining dependency
+
+An actual issue #62 submission is still required: contributor-controlled producer
+implementation and test keys, source/licence/toolchain/method disclosure and
+maintainer-side reproduction. An external consumer is also needed for the reverse
+lane. The adapter permits native consumer results without importing reference
+verification code; optional mapped projections report agreement or divergence
+only. This work creates no new challenge, normative schema, v0.1 result, public
+push, PR, issue/comment, release or EXTERNAL_EVIDENCE entry.
+
+The five-artifact transport currently excludes profiles and witnesses. External
+adapters execute locally without a sandbox; their declared source hash is not
+authorship or dependency-closure attestation. The local observer uses a public
+test policy. Linux x86-64 CPython 3.12 wheels are the reproduced platform. Complete
+limitations and machine-readable records are in run_record.json.
+
+## Complete archived payloads
+
+To keep the review compact, all measurement payloads and logs are retained in
+`evidence/payloads.tar.gz`, with per-file hashes in `evidence/PAYLOAD_SHA256SUMS`.
+The final signed lifecycle, policies, final command streams and run records remain
+directly readable; duplicate generated bundles, raw contribution logs and negative
+fixtures (including deliberately trailing whitespace) are in the archive unchanged.
+
+Restore every captured relative path and verify every payload hash:
+
+```sh
+mkdir /tmp/k2-evidence-restored
+tar -xzf interop/same-version/v0.2.0-beta.1/evidence/payloads.tar.gz -C /tmp/k2-evidence-restored
+# From /tmp/k2-evidence-restored, use the absolute path to the checksum file:
+sha256sum -c /ABSOLUTE/REPO/interop/same-version/v0.2.0-beta.1/evidence/PAYLOAD_SHA256SUMS
+```
+
+The run records retain original execution paths and hashes. The archive preserves
+payload contents, not runtime environments. Reproduce tools with the documented
+commands and frozen dependency bundles.
+
+## Projection validation review correction
+
+The review found a real defect in the external consumer transport: a supplied
+`observation` with null `records`, `reconciliation_summary` and `checks` passed the
+former shallow check and was recorded as REPORTED / PROJECTION_DIVERGES. The fix
+validates nested types, exact fields, pinned class/observer/reason/check/state
+vocabularies, structured subjects, ordering and summary counts/status consistency
+before REPORTED. Malformed projections now yield
+ADAPTER_ERROR / MALFORMED_COMPARISON_PROJECTION. Absent/null observation still
+yields NOT_COMPARABLE, and a valid reported divergence remains distinguishable.
+
+[Review reproduction](evidence/projection-validation-fix/review-reproduction.json)
+captures actual adapter subprocesses against the before/fixed code and the real
+previous projection. They are local test doubles, not outside consumer evidence.
+[Current tests and commands](evidence/projection-validation-fix/validation.json)
+record 28 successful tests, including null nested structures, malformed record,
+status, count and check fields, pinned reason channels and a valid actual projection.
+[New pinned measurement](evidence/projection-validation-fix/measurement/run_record.json)
+confirms the full local reference result is unchanged: five authenticated records,
+Python/Node parity, eight expected negative controls and INCOMPLETE reconciliation.
+External result remains EXTERNAL_RESULT_NOT_SUPPLIED.
+
+The original measurement files and their original payload archive are unchanged.
+Prior root summaries/source hashes are retained under
+`evidence/projection-validation-fix/before/`. All new measurement payloads and logs
+are retained in `evidence/projection-validation-fix/measurement.tar.gz`, with
+`MEASUREMENT_SHA256SUMS`; extract this archive into a fresh directory to restore
+the `measurement/` tree. The original 56-command beta suite was not repeated:
+the frozen release tools, normative target and dependencies did not change.
