+# Same-version role matrix
+
+All cells target v0.2.0-beta.1 / 8a6c01ecce457aa94330c0ed7219e4c56ebfe771.
+`pins.json.target` also binds the exact five normative documents and all schemas.
+Evidence against v0.1.2 is not added to these results.
+
+| Lane | Producer | Consumer | Current evidence | Permitted conclusion |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| Reference → reference | Pinned Python example, public test keys | Pinned Python verifier/reconciler; pinned Node verifier parity | Local measured run | Local regression behavior only |
+| External → reference | Contributor adapter and its source/key evidence | Pinned Python verifier/reconciler | EXTERNAL_RESULT_NOT_SUPPLIED | No external producer claim |
+| Reference → external | Exact reference bundle bytes | Contributor's own consumer logic | EXTERNAL_RESULT_NOT_SUPPLIED | No external consumer claim |
+| External → external | Contributor producer bundle | Contributor consumer adapter over that same bundle | EXTERNAL_RESULT_NOT_SUPPLIED | No interchange claim |
+
+The reference implementation ID begins `reference:` and cannot be used as an
+external adapter ID. Producer and consumer transport roles are explicit and
+checked both before invocation and in the response. Labels, separate commands,
+languages or keys do not establish independent authorship. All external adapter
+records keep `independence: NOT_ASSESSED` even when projections agree.
+
+Within a lifecycle, issuer dispatch and receiver receipt must occupy their
+respective Control roles. Separate artifact families, record references and
+chain identities remain the release verifier/reconciler's responsibility.
+The harness's five-artifact gate is a transport guard, not an alternative schema
+validator. Unchanged serialized bytes are hashed before and after consumption.
+
+The local Effect is accepted as independent only under the published demonstration
+test policy. Removing that policy yields `observer_assessment: unknown`. That
+internal evidence-class result does not describe the independence of the software
+authors or establish an external observer.
