@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+{
+  "accessed_at_utc": "2026-11-02T19:08:31.114Z",
+  "method": "GitHub connector github_fetch_issue / github_fetch_issue_comments",
+  "issue": {
+    "issue": {
+      "url": "https://github.com/halvrenofviryel/ai-runtime-evidence-protocol/issues/62",
+      "title": "Independent v0.2 producer challenge — emit and verify a release-pinned minimal lifecycle",
+      "issue_number": 62,
+      "body": "## Objective\n\nIndependently implement the smallest useful AIREP v0.2 producer that emits a release-pinned Decision → Control → Execution → Effect lifecycle, then run the published verification and reconciliation paths over its output.\n\nThis is an evidence-gathering challenge, not a requirement to reproduce the first-party producer and not a request for a complete AIREP product.\n\n## Exact target\n\n- Release: `v0.2.0-beta.1`\n- Tag target commit: `8a6c01ecce457aa94330c0ed7219e4c56ebfe771`\n- Normative entry point: `spec/airep/v0.2/SPEC.md` at that tag\n- Schemas: `spec/airep/v0.2/schemas/` at that tag\n- Verification inputs and rules: `spec/airep/v0.2/VERIFICATION.md`, `INTEGRITY.md`, `CONFORMANCE_CLASSES.md`, and `RECONCILIATION.md` at that tag\n\nDo not target moving `main`, and do not combine this result with the frozen v0.1.2 external-producer result.\n\n## Minimal scope\n\nImplement a producer in one language not copied from the first-party Python producer—Go, Rust, or TypeScript are particularly welcome—that emits the five-artifact minimal lifecycle:\n\n1. Decision\n2. issuer Control dispatch\n3. receiver Control receipt\n4. Execution\n5. Effect\n\nThe artifacts should use contributor-controlled test keys and should be checkable with two top-level commands:\n\n```text\n<producer command>     # writes the lifecycle and required verification inputs\n<verification command> # runs the release-pinned verifier/reconciler and retains output\n```\n\nExact command syntax is up to the implementation. No private service, credential, or deployment is required.\n\n## Evidence bundle\n\nPlease provide:\n\n- implementation source and licence;\n- exact runtime/toolchain versions;\n- exact commands and complete stdout/stderr;\n- generated artifacts and any bindings, revocation input, independence policy, or profile basis used;\n- SHA-256 identities for the source snapshot and submitted artifacts;\n- the release-pinned verifier and reconciliation outputs;\n- a short method note describing whether first-party producer code was read or reused.\n\nThe maintainer will reproduce the submitted bundle before any result is summarized in `EXTERNAL_EVIDENCE.md`.\n\n## Valid outcomes\n\nAny of these is useful:\n\n- **compatible** — the pinned verifier/reconciler accepts and classifies the submitted lifecycle as expected;\n- **divergence found** — independently generated bytes expose a verifier, producer, or expected-result mismatch;\n- **spec ambiguity found** — two reasonable readings of the frozen text produce different results.\n\nPASS is not required. A reproducible failure or ambiguity is evidence, not a failed contribution.\n\n## Claim boundary\n\nOne successful submission would be one independently authored producer result against this exact beta target. It would not by itself establish general interchange, deployment interoperability, protocol correctness, AIREP stability, or standards-body endorsement. Contributor credit will be added only with permission and after maintainer-side reproduction.\n",
+      "state": "open",
+      "user": {
+        "login": "halvrenofviryel",
+        "name": "halvrenofviryel",
+        "email": null,
+        "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/246127299?v=4",
+        "id": 246127299
+      },
+      "assignees": null,
+      "labels": [
+        {
+          "name": "help wanted",
+          "color": "008672",
+          "description": "Extra attention is needed"
+        },
+        {
+          "name": "adoption",
+          "color": "0e8a16",
+          "description": ""
